ount token (in-cluster) | kube-apiserver | RBAC enforced via odh-model-controller-role ClusterRole; SA odh-model-controller |\n277\t| Kubernetes API | REST | ServiceAccount token (in-cluster) | kube-apiserver | RBAC enforced via model-serving-api ClusterRole; SA model-serving-api |\n278\t| :8443/metrics | GET | TokenReview + SubjectAccessReview (controller-runtime authn/authz filter) | controller-runtime metrics authn/authz filter | RBAC via proxy-role; exposed by Service odh-model-controller-metrics-service; TLS certificate provisioned by OpenShift service-ca |\n279\t| :8443/healthz | GET | None | N/A | Unauthenticated Kubernetes liveness probe endpoint |\n280\t| :8443/readyz | GET | None | N/A | Unauthenticated Kubernetes readiness probe endpoint |\n281\t| /metrics | Unknown | None | N/A | HTTPS metrics endpoint on port 8080 via promhttp.Handler; no authentication middleware; TLS via model-serving-api certificate |\n282\t| Operator webhook | CREATE | Kubernetes admission | ValidatingWebhookConfiguration | Admission validation |\n283\t| /api/v1/gateways | All | Bearer token | middleware.Auth | Bearer token extracted from Authorization header; 401 returned for missing or invalid token |\n284\t| /api/v1/samples/llm-d | All | None | N/A | Static public YAML templates; unauthenticated by design |\n285\t\n286\t### Security Evidence\n287\t\n288\t| Kind | Target | Detail | Signal Type |\n289\t|----|------|------|-----------|\n290\t| tls-config | crypto/tls | TLS configuration import | dependency-signal |\n291\t| rbac-ref | SelfSubjectAccessReviews | Token or subject access review call | literal |\n292\t\n293\t### FIPS Compliance\n294\t\n295\t#### Build-Time FIPS (check-payload gate)\n296\t\n297\t| Aspect | Value | Source |\n298\t|--------|-------|--------|\n299\t| **Build flags** | `CGO_ENABLED=1 GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime -tags strictfipsruntime` | Dockerfile.konflux:28 |\n300\t| **Linking** | Dynamic (CGO_ENABLED=1) | Dockerfile.konflux:28 |\n301\t| **OpenSSL in image** | Yes (via UBI9 ubi-minimal base) | Dockerfile.konflux:30 |\n302\t| **OLM FIPS annotation** | not extracted | unknown |\n303\t\n304\t#### Application-Level Crypto\n305\t\n306\t| Aspect | Value | Source |\n307\t|--------|-------|--------|\n308\t| **TLS configuration** | Uses crypto/tls with cipher suites resolved from OpenShift APIServer TLS profile; defaults to Mozilla Intermediate (TLS 1.2+, ECDHE+AES-GCM/ChaCha20 only) | pkg/tls/tls.go:38-60, 141-145 |\n309\t| **Crypto libraries** | stdlib crypto/tls (FIPS via strictfipsruntime OpenSSL backend) | cmd/main.go:181, server/server.go:4, pkg/tls/tls.go:21 |\n310\t| **Certificate handling** | OpenShift service-ca provisioned TLS secrets with runtime cert reloading via fsnotify | server/main.go:68-81, config/server/server.yaml:1 |\n311\t| **Non-FIPS crypto risks** | None detected; all configured cipher suites are FIPS-approved (AES-GCM, ChaCha20-Poly1305 via ECDHE key exchange) | pkg/tls/tls.go:53-60 |\n312\t\n313\tThe build uses `GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime` with `-tags strictfipsruntime`, which enforces FIPS-validated cryptography via the Go runtime's OpenSSL backend. The application-level TLS configuration exclusively uses FIPS-approved cipher suites from the Mozilla Intermediate set. The `pkg/tls` package maps OpenSSL cipher names to Go constants and only includes ECDHE-based ciphers with AES-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305, all of which are FIPS 140-2/140-3 approved when backed by OpenSSL. [source: Dockerfile.konflux:28, pkg/tls/tls.go:38-60]\n314\t## Admission Webhooks\n315\t\n316\t| Name | Type | Path | Port | Failure Policy | Resources | Operations | Purpose |\n317\t|----|----|----|----|--------------|---------|----------|-------|\n318\t| mutating.pod.odh-model-controller.opendatahub.io | Mutating | /mutate--v1-pod |  | Fail | pods | CREATE |  |\n319\t| minferencegraph-v1alpha1.odh-model-controller.opendatahub.io | Mutating | /mutate-serving-kserve-io-v1alpha1-inferencegraph |  | Fail | inferencegraphs | CREATE 