priority exception (strategy frontmatter `priority: Critical` → P0), not via priority inheritance.\n\n## Non-HLR unknowns — why they are not Investigation epics\n\n- \"KEDA ScaledObject with idleReplicaCount: 0 correctly pauses and resumes\" (assumption, needs validation): implementation approach is fixed by the upstream design; failure would be fix-and-retry → acceptance criteria on E002 (scale-to-zero / scale-from-zero integration tests).\n- \"EPP flow control queue metrics available at zero replicas\" (assumption, needs validation): changes documentation recommendations, not which epics exist or what the controller does → scope + acceptance criteria on E004 (validated example trigger configurations).\n- \"Target p50/p95 for scale-from-zero\" (open question, llm-d team): an input to documentation content (headroom recommendations), not to epic structure → E004 scope/stakeholder input.\n- \"Prometheus capacity guidance for fleet scale\" (open question, PSAP): documentation content input → E004 scope/stakeholder input.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nEvaluated per Step 5.5 / Rule 21: the only external dependency with uncertain timing is upstream PR kserve/kserve#5839. A viable fallback exists (RHOAI carries the patch downstream with backport once merged), so the dependency is modeled as an acceptance criterion and risk on E002 (consume upstream, or carry the patch) rather than a separate upstream epic or a Tier 1/Tier 2 split. No tiered delivery split.\n\n## Health Warnings (non-blocking)\n\n1. **Upstream timing risk**: kserve/kserve#5839 is open and in progress; if it stalls, E002 timeline slips unless the patch-carry fallback is exercised. Mitigation captured as an E002 acceptance criterion and risk.\n2. **External content inputs to documentation**: E004 requires inputs from teams outside this strategy (llm-d team for the scale-from-zero p50/p95 target; Performance/PSAP for Prometheus capacity guidance). These are stakeholder commitments, not schedule gates the docs team