# Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. An analysis document exists that enumerates, item by item, the downstream adaptation kserve/kserve#5839 requires beyond the odh-model-controller authentication context, with each item classified as covered or additional.\n2. The integration recommendation (upstream merge vs. patch carry, with backport notes) is stated with rationale grounded in the PR's current status.\n3. Potential RBAC and TLS adjustments for OpenShift are explicitly assessed — needed or not, and where each would land.\n4. The findings are reviewed with the Serving team and the outcome recorded, so the standalone KEDA implementation scope can be finalized from it.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nNo HLR is directly implemented by this epic. It resolves the strategy open question that gates the scope of the standalone KEDA implementation covering HLR-1 through HLR-6; its outcome determines whether that implementation scope needs rewriting.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":96920,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f4cc6a4428f1cc4","agent_id":"aa54ef1391fcef3a7","session_id":"207785e0-7a4d-4b13-b5f6-b50ef683c695","uuid":"e7410b60-e956-446a-8d6e-7bda95cd02fb","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:52:11.037Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8008"}
