{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ee8a08bc-92a4-4ad3-9ef5-20b456419776","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7b2de92154798f9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8008-3w537q7v/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8008-E002.md","content":"# Standalone KEDA autoscaling path for LLMInferenceService in the llmisvc-controller\n\n## Description\n\nDeliver standalone KEDA autoscaling as a first-class path for LLMInferenceService in the RHOAI kserve llmisvc-controller, alongside the existing WVA-mediated path, following the upstream design kserve/kserve#5646 and implementation PR kserve/kserve#5839. Users configure KEDA triggers directly in the LLMInferenceService spec without deploying WVA, bringing feature parity with v1beta1 InferenceService. This epic covers the API surface, CEL validation, controller reconciliation branching, and scaling status conditions for both paths, including scale-to-zero, scale-from-zero, and disaggregated prefill/decode scaling.\n\n## Scope\n\n- API type changes in `pkg/apis/serving/v1alpha2/llm_inference_service_types.go`: a standalone KEDA spec at the ScalingSpec level containing `pollingInterval`, `cooldownPeriod`, and a `triggers` field for user-defined KEDA trigger definitions (type, metadata map).\n- Validation changes in `pkg/apis/serving/v1alpha2/llm_inference_service_validation.go`: relax the CEL rule from requiring `wva` to requiring at least one of `wva` or `keda` when `spec.scaling` is configured; enforce at-most-one (mutual exclusivity between the two paths), mutual exclusivity with static `spec.replicas`, and trigger completeness. For disaggregated deployments, both prefill and decode phases must use the same scaling path to maintain actuator consistency (architecture overlay 0011).\n- Controller changes in `pkg/controller/v1alpha2/llmisvc/scaling.go`: branch on which path is configured — the standalone KEDA path creates a ScaledObject from user-provided triggers (Resource, External, and PodMetric trigger types, per the v1beta1 reference reconciler at `pkg/controller/v1beta1/inferenceservice/reconcilers/keda/keda_reconciler.go`) and skips VariantAutoscaling CR creation entirely.\n- Scale-to-zero via KEDA `idleReplicaCount: 0` for both paths, releasing GPU capacity when deployments are idle; scale-from-zero in the standalone path driven by user-configured triggers (e.g., Prometheus queries on EPP flow control queue metrics); independent per-phase scaling for disaggregated deployments via phase-specific ScaledObjects.\n- Scaling status conditions and scaling-decision events for both paths (KEDA ScaledObject events for the standalone path; WVA events for the WVA path) so operators can observe scaling with signal attribution.\n- Backwards compatibility: static deployments with no autoscaling configured behave identically, and existing CRs with `spec.scaling.wva` continue unchanged — the standalone KEDA path is additive.\n- Integration tests for standalone KEDA across two topologies (integrated and disaggregated).\n- Upstream alignment: consume kserve/kserve#5839 once merged; if the PR is delayed, carry the patch downstream with backport.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. Given an LLMInferenceService with `spec.scaling.keda` configured with user-defined triggers and no WVA deployed, when the trigger condition is met (e.g., Prometheus query threshold exceeded), then the deployment scales up — measured by KEDA ScaledObject status showing active and Deployment replica count increasing.\n2. Given an LLMInferenceService with both `spec.scaling.wva` and `spec.scaling.keda` set, when the CR is submitted, then the API server rejects it with a CEL validation error indicating mutual exclusivity; a `spec.scaling` block with neither path present is likewise rejected (at-least-one).\n3. Given an LLMInferenceService with `spec.scaling.keda` and no `spec.scaling.wva`, when the llmisvc-controller reconciles, then no VariantAutoscaling CR is created and a ScaledObject with the user-provided triggers is created — measured by `kubectl get variantautoscalings` returning empty and `kubectl get scaledobjects` returning a ScaledObject with the user's triggers.\n4. Given an LLMInferenceService with KEDA and `idleReplicaCount: 0` (either path), when no requests are received for the cooldown period, then the deployment scales to zero — measured by Deployment replica count reaching 0 and KEDA ScaledObject status showing idle; when a trigger subsequently fires, the deployment scales back up and serves requests (scale-from-zero).\n5. Given a disaggregated LLMInferenceService with separate scaling configs (either path), when prefill pods reach saturation while decode pods remain below threshold, then only the prefill pool scales up — measured by independent scaling resource status for prefill and decode roles; validation rejects disaggregated deployments that mix scaling paths across phases.\n6. Given a deployment with autoscaling active (either path), when Prometheus metrics become unavailable, then the deployment holds its current replica count — measured by replica count remaining stable during the metric outage.\n7. Static deployments with no autoscaling configured continue to serve identically — measured by no VariantAutoscaling, HPA, or ScaledObject resources created for deployments without `spec.scaling`; existing CRs with `spec.scaling.wva` produce identical resources as before the change.\n8. Scaling events are visible to operators with signal attribution for both paths — measured by KEDA ScaledObject events for the standalone path and WVA events for the WVA path, with scaling status conditions reflecting the active path.\n9. Integration tests pass for the standalone KEDA path across both topologies (integrated and disaggregated), including scale-to-zero and scale-from-zero cycles.\n10. The delivered changes are consistent with kserve/kserve#5839 (consumed from upstream), or the patch is carried downstream with a documented backport plan if the upstream PR is delayed.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 [P0]: LLMInferenceService supports standalone KEDA autoscaling with user-defined triggers without requiring WVA deployment (kserve/kserve#5646).\n- HLR-2 [P0]: The two autoscaling paths are mutually exclusive at the API level with CEL validation enforcing at-least-one and at-most-one.\n- HLR-3 [P0]: Scale-to-zero — idle deployments scale to zero replicas via KEDA `idleReplicaCount: 0` (both paths).\n- HLR-4 [P0]: Scale-from-zero — deployments at zero replicas scale up to serve incoming requests (standalone KEDA via user-configured triggers).\n- HLR-5 [P0]: Disaggregated prefill and decode pools scale independently based on their respective load profiles (both paths).\n- HLR-6 [P1]: Scaling events visible to operators with signal attribution (KEDA ScaledObject events for the standalone path; WVA events for the WVA path). Deliberately bundled with the P0 work: it shares the same controller, status-condition, and event surface, so splitting it would build the same surface twice.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":97655,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f4cc6a4428f1cc4","agent_id":"aa54ef1391fcef3a7","session_id":"207785e0-7a4d-4b13-b5f6-b50ef683c695","uuid":"2e4ac1da-8ba5-4d76-b5c1-b881585905ef","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:52:34.536Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8008"}
