enticated Prometheus triggers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. Given an LLMInferenceService configured for standalone KEDA with Prometheus-type triggers, when odh-model-controller reconciles, then the per-namespace authentication context exists — ServiceAccount, ServiceAccountToken Secret, Role/RoleBinding, and TriggerAuthentication CR — owned by the LLMInferenceService.\n2. Given a KEDA Prometheus trigger that references the TriggerAuthentication resource, when KEDA queries Thanos/Prometheus, then the query succeeds using the ServiceAccount bearer token over TLS 1.2+ — measured by the authenticated query returning metrics.\n3. Given an LLMInferenceService whose standalone KEDA configuration is removed, when reconciliation completes, then the authentication resources are cleaned up through the owner-reference lifecycle.\n4. Existing v1beta1 InferenceService KEDA authentication behavior is unchanged — measured by the existing reconciler's tests passing and no resource changes for v1beta1 InferenceServices.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 [P0] (OpenShift enablement): LLMInferenceService supports standalone KEDA autoscaling with user-defined triggers without requiring WVA deployment — the primary supported trigger source (Prometheus/Thanos) requires this authentication context on OpenShift.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":99312,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f4cc6a4428f1cc4","agent_id":"aa54ef1391fcef3a7","session_id":"207785e0-7a4d-4b13-b5f6-b50ef683c695","uuid":"9a5e5f43-6991-4af5-9da0-8c7fc2ce9fb4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:52:45.992Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8008"}
