ical \"KServe\" component; the llmisvc-controller is the serving control-plane orchestrator for LLMInferenceService, which is the closest canonical bucket.\n52\t- \"odh-model-controller\" → `Serving Orchestration` — same serving control-plane subsystem; kept as a separate epic because it is a distinct repo and logical change.\n53\t- \"Documentation\" → `Documentation` — verbatim match.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n56\t\n57\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n58\t|-----|----------|---------|\n59\t| HLR-1: LLMInferenceService supports standalone KEDA autoscaling with user-defined triggers without requiring WVA deployment | P0 | E002, E003 |\n60\t| HLR-2: Two autoscaling paths mutually exclusive at API level; CEL validation enforcing at-least-one and at-most-one | P0 | E002 |\n61\t| HLR-3: Scale-to-zero via KEDA `idleReplicaCount: 0` (both paths) | P0 | E002 |\n62\t| HLR-4: Scale-from-zero (WVA via EPP queue metrics; standalone KEDA via user-configured triggers) | P0 | E002, E004 (trigger guidance) |\n63\t| HLR-5: Disaggregated prefill and decode pools scale independently | P0 | E002 |\n64\t| HLR-6: Scaling events visible to operators with signal attribution | P1 | E002 |\n65\t| HLR-7: Well-lit path documentation with decision guide, recipes, troubleshooting | P1 | E004 |\n66\t\n67\tFull coverage; no orphaned HLRs.\n68\t\n69\t### Priority decisions\n70\t\n71\t- P1 HLR-6 (scaling events / signal attribution) stays bundled in E002: it shares the same controller, status-condition, and event surface as the P0 work — it is not a distinct, deferrable feature with independent surfaces, and splitting it would make two epics build the same status surface.\n72\t- E004 (docs-authoring) is P0 via the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy frontmatter `priority: Critical` → P0), not via priority inheritance; per Rule 11 its edges do not push priority upstream.\n73\t- E001 is P0 by priority inheritance: it blocks all P0 implementation work.\n74\t\n75\t## Unknowns evaluated