risk on E002.\n89\t2. **External content inputs to documentation**: E004 requires inputs from teams outside this strategy — the llm-d team (scale-from-zero p50/p95 target) and Performance/PSAP (Prometheus capacity guidance). These are stakeholder commitments the docs team does not control; a human should secure them early.\n90\t3. **Proposed acceptance criteria / pending process gates**: the strategy marks its ACs as \"Proposed — requires PM/Engineering validation\", and all Prerequisites & Process Gates (architecture review, build onboarding, license validation, etc.) are \"Pending human review\". The decomposition proceeds on the proposed ACs; that human validation remains outstanding.\n91\t4. **No RHOAI-specific scalability target**: the NFR section flags that no target exists for concurrent ScaledObjects; capacity guidance is deferred to documentation (E004) — a potential scope trap if a hard target is later imposed.\n92\t\n93\t## Scope Notes\n94\t\n95\t- Integration testing across standalone KEDA x 2 topologies (integrated and disaggregated) is folded into E002/E003 acceptance criteria rather than a separate epic: the strategy's Impacted Teams table lists no separate QE team, and testing has no separate component boundary here.\n96\t- The strategy is additive (standalone KEDA alongside WVA), not a capability replacement, so no feature-flag/rollback epic is generated (Rule 23); backwards compatibility for static deployments and existing `spec.scaling.wva` CRs is enforced as E002 acceptance criteria, with CEL mutual-exclusivity validation as the guard.\n97\t- No onboarding chain is generated (Rule 20): kserve and odh-model-controller both exist in the platform (architecture context files present), and Documentation needs no repo onboarding.\n98\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-984475b99c625cd7","agent_id":"ac4122934639fa38c","session_id":"207785e0-7a4d-4b13-b5f6-b50ef683c695","uuid":"13d5efd1-1f6e-4efe-a8e6-5ca9fbb4048d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:58:24.