{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a3ba5afe3786289","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8008-E003\n3\ttitle: KEDA TriggerAuthentication reconciler for LLMInferenceService standalone KEDA\n4\t  Prometheus triggers\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8008\n6\tcomponent: Serving Orchestration\n7\tteam: Serving team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8008-E002\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 0\n18\t  external_dependency: 0\n19\t  human_process_gates: 0\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 6\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# KEDA TriggerAuthentication reconciler for LLMInferenceService standalone KEDA Prometheus triggers\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tProvide the downstream authentication context that KEDA Prometheus-type triggers need on OpenShift for LLMInferenceService standalone KEDA autoscaling: a parallel reconciler flow in odh-model-controller that creates per-namespace authentication resources — a dedicated ServiceAccount, a ServiceAccountToken Secret, a Role/RoleBinding for metrics access, and a KEDA TriggerAuthentication CR supplying bearer token and CA cert to KEDA's Prometheus triggers — following the existing `kserve_keda_reconciler` pattern used for v1beta1 InferenceService KEDA autoscaling.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- A new reconciler flow in odh-model-controller, alongside the existing `internal/controller/serving/reconcilers/kserve_keda_reconciler.go`, that reacts to LLMInferenceService resources configured for standalone KEDA with Prometheus-type triggers.\n40\t- Create the per-namespace authentication resources: dedicated ServiceAccount (`inference-prometheus-auth` pattern), ServiceAccountToken Secret (`kubernetes.io/service-account-token` type), Role/RoleBinding for metrics access, and the KEDA TriggerAuthentication CR.\n41\t- Reuse the existing reconciler's conventions for resource naming, owner reference management, and lifecycle cleanup, so the authentication resources are garbage-collected when the LLMInferenceService KEDA configuration is removed.\n42\t- No changes to the existing v1beta1 InferenceService KEDA authentication flow (no regression).\n43\t- Integration coverage for the LLMInferenceService standalone KEDA topology using authenticated Prometheus triggers.\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t1. Given an LLMInferenceService configured for standalone KEDA with Prometheus-type triggers, when odh-model-controller reconciles, then the per-namespace authentication context exists — ServiceAccount, ServiceAccountToken Secret, Role/RoleBinding, and TriggerAuthentication CR — owned by the LLMInferenceService.\n48\t2. Given a KEDA Prometheus trigger that references the TriggerAuthentication resource, when KEDA queries Thanos/Prometheus, then the query succeeds using the ServiceAccount bearer token over TLS 1.2+ — measured by the authenticated query returning metrics.\n49\t3. Given an LLMInferenceService whose standalone KEDA configuration is removed, when reconciliation completes, then the authentication resources are cleaned up through the owner-reference lifecycle.\n50\t4. Existing v1beta1 InferenceService KEDA authentication behavior is unchanged — measured by the existing reconciler's tests passing and no resource changes for v1beta1 InferenceServices.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- HLR-1 [P0] (OpenShift enablement): LLMInferenceService supports standalone KEDA autoscaling with user-defined triggers without requiring WVA deployment — the primary supported trigger source (Prometheus/Thanos) requires this authentication context on OpenShift.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f5be360b42a61fc","agent_id":"a074c867882eb1171","session_id":"207785e0-7a4d-4b13-b5f6-b50ef683c695","uuid":"9ae0f5d4-08f3-4f61-b400-d6eb72f5bf99","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:59:38.853Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a3ba5afe3786289","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8008 decomposition"}
