{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab87063ba59b84b0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8008-E004\n3\ttitle: 'LLMInferenceService autoscaling documentation: decision guide, recipes, troubleshooting'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8008\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: Documentation team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8008-E002\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8008-E003\n13\tai_signals:\n14\t  change_specificity: 1\n15\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n16\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n17\t  existing_foundation: 1\n18\t  open_questions: -1\n19\t  external_dependency: 0\n20\t  human_process_gates: -1\n21\t  repo_access: 1\n22\t  architecture_claims: 1\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 3\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# LLMInferenceService autoscaling documentation: decision guide, recipes, troubleshooting\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tAuthor the well-lit path documentation for LLMInferenceService autoscaling covering both autoscaling paths — WVA-mediated and standalone KEDA — plus static allocation: a decision guide, configuration recipes per workload shape, troubleshooting, and a supported configuration matrix. Includes KEDA prerequisite installation guidance, recommended scale-from-zero trigger configurations using EPP flow control queue metrics, and TriggerAuthentication reference guidance for authenticated Prometheus/Thanos queries on OpenShift.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Decision guide covering the three allocation approaches — WVA-mediated autoscaling, standalone KEDA, and static allocation — with use-case-based recommendations (e.g., a coding assistant deployment that scales prefill and decode pools during business hours and releases GPUs overnight).\n40\t- Configuration recipes per workload shape covering both autoscaling paths, scale-to-zero (`idleReplicaCount: 0`) and scale-from-zero, including disaggregated prefill/decode deployments; recommended scale-from-zero trigger configurations using EPP flow control queue metrics, with example ScaledObject templates.\n41\t- Guidance for operators to reference the TriggerAuthentication resource in their KEDA trigger definitions for authenticated Prometheus/Thanos queries on OpenShift.\n42\t- KEDA documented as a prerequisite with installation guidance referencing the GitOps repository (ODH-ADR-0007; RHOAI does not auto-install external operator dependencies — platform policy overlay 0008).\n43\t- Supported configuration matrix and troubleshooting paths, including misconfigured scale-from-zero triggers (requests waiting indefinitely at the EPP) and behavior during Prometheus metric outages.\n44\t- Scale-from-zero latency expectations and headroom pre-scaling recommendations for latency-sensitive workloads, incorporating the target p50/p95 to be confirmed with the llm-d team (the RFE references a 60-second p50 threshold), and referencing the fast model startup RFEs (RHAIRFE-7753, RHAIRFE-7599, RHAIRFE-7139). If the confirmation is outstanding at authoring time, the known 60-second p50 reference is documented with TBD markers for the confirmed target.\n45\t- Prometheus capacity guidance for fleet-scale deployments (KEDA polling intervals at scale), incorporating Performance/PSAP team input. If that input is outstanding at authoring time, the guidance is authored from the known KEDA polling behavior with TBD markers for the Performance/PSAP-confirmed figures.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t1. The decision guide covers all three allocation approaches (WVA-mediated, standalone KEDA, static) with use-case-based recommendations for choosing between them.\n50\t2. Configuration recipes exist for both autoscaling paths across representative workload shapes, including disaggregated prefill/decode deployments.\n51\t3. Example ScaledObject templates for scale-from-zero using EPP flow control queue metrics are provided and validated against the implemented behavior, including metric availability when pods are at zero replicas and EPP remains running.\n52\t4. Documentation instructs operators to reference the TriggerAuthentication resource in KEDA trigger definitions for authenticated Prometheus/Thanos queries on OpenShift.\n53\t5. KEDA installation is documented as a prerequisite, referencing the GitOps repository.\n54\t6. The supported configuration matrix and troubleshooting section cover invalid scaling-path combinations (CEL mutual-exclusivity errors), misconfigured scale-from-zero triggers, and metric-outage behavior.\n55\t7. Scale-from-zero latency expectations and headroom pre-scaling recommendations are documented. If the llm-d team has confirmed a p50/p95 target, the documented expectations incorporate it; if the confirmation is outstanding at authoring time, the currently known 60-second p50 reference (RFE telemetry threshold) is documented with TBD markers for the confirmed target — the AC is satisfiable either way.\n56\t8. Prometheus capacity guidance for fleet-scale deployments is included. If Performance/PSAP team input has arrived, the guidance incorporates it; if it is outstanding at authoring time, the guidance is authored from the known KEDA polling behavior (configurable poll intervals, Prometheus load at fleet scale) with TBD markers for the Performance/PSAP-confirmed figures — the AC is satisfiable either way.\n57\t9. All content is technically reviewed against the implemented autoscaling paths — engineering review of the documented behavior, commands, and example manifests.\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability\n60\t\n61\t- HLR-7 [P1]: Well-lit path documentation covers both autoscaling paths with decision guide, configuration recipes per workload shape, and troubleshooting.\n62\t- HLR-4 [P0] (guidance aspect): Scale-from-zero via user-configured triggers — recommended trigger configurations and example ScaledObject templates.\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f5be360b42a61fc","agent_id":"a074c867882eb1171","session_id":"207785e0-7a4d-4b13-b5f6-b50ef683c695","uuid":"f127c61c-017e-4bc2-a620-b1749669d839","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:59:39.569Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab87063ba59b84b0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8008 decomposition"}
