{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9324ac5bd5ef0eb7","type":"tool_result","content":"118:| github.com/kserve/kserve | v0.17.0-rc1 | Yes |  | Go module dependency |\n16:**Detailed**: KServe provides the core model serving infrastructure for RHOAI, managing inference workloads from single-model deployments through multi-model inference graphs and LLM-optimized serving. The platform is composed of four main controller binaries — the core kserve manager (InferenceService, InferenceGraph, TrainedModel), the LLMInferenceService controller (llmisvc), the local model caching controllers (localmodel/localmodelnode), and the kserve-module operator that manages component installation on OpenShift. Each controller reconciles its CRDs and owns downstream Kubernetes resources (Deployments, Services, HTTPRoutes, PersistentVolumes) through controller-runtime watches. The repository also ships a Python SDK (`kserve` package) with framework-specific model servers (HuggingFace, sklearn, XGBoost, LightGBM, vLLM, and others) that implement the KServe V2 Inference Protocol via both HTTP (FastAPI/uvicorn) and gRPC endpoints. An inference router binary provides authenticated request routing for InferenceGraph DAGs, enforcing access control via Kubernetes TokenReview and SubjectAccessReview APIs. [source: cmd/manager/main.go:288, cmd/llmisvc/main.go:339, cmd/router/main.go:525, kserve-module/cmd/kserve-module/main.go:91, python/kserve/kserve/protocol/grpc/grpc_predict_v2.proto:23]\n22:**Controller topology.** The `manager` binary reconciles the foundational CRDs — InferenceService, InferenceGraph, ClusterServingRuntime, and TrainedModel — creating Deployments, Services, and ingress resources (HTTPRoutes, Istio VirtualServices, or OpenShift Routes depending on platform configuration). The `llmisvc` controller handles the LLMInferenceService and LLMInferenceServiceConfig CRDs with extensive Gateway API integration, managing HorizontalPodAutoscalers, LeaderWorkerSets for multi-node inference, KEDA ScaledObjects, and InferencePool resources for gateway-based load balancing. The `localmodel`/`localmodelnode` pair manages persistent model caching at cluster and node level through PersistentVolume/PersistentVolumeClaim lifecycle and batch Job-based model downloads. The `kserve-module` operator runs from a separate Go module (`kserve-module/`) and manages the installation and configuration of all other KServe components on the ODH/RHOAI platform, watching the `Kserve` CR from `components.platform.opendatahub.io`. [source: pkg/controller/v1beta1/inferenceservice/controller.go:724, pkg/controller/v1alpha2/llmisvc/controller.go:419, pkg/controller/v1alpha1/localmodel/reconcilers/localmodelcache_reconciler.go:365, kserve-module/pkg/kservemodule/setup.go:68]\n30:**Internal platform dependencies.** The kserve-module operator depends on `odh-platform-utilities` for platform detection, manifest rendering, and deployment helpers. The LLMInferenceService controller integrates with the Gateway API Inference Extension (`sigs.k8s.io/gateway-api-inference-extension`) for InferencePool type conversion, enabling gateway-based routing of inference traffic. Gateway API watches are conditional — the controller checks for CRD availability before registering watches — allowing graceful degradation when Gateway API is not installed. cert-manager integration provides automated TLS certificate management through Certificate and ClusterIssuer CRDs. [source: kserve-module/pkg/apis/v1alpha1/types.go:9, pkg/apis/gie/v1alpha2pool/inferencepool_conversion.go:29, pkg/controller/v1alpha2/llmisvc/controller.go:444]\n56:| LLMInferenceService controller | Controller | Reconciles LLMInferenceService resources |\n57:| LLMInferenceServiceConfig controller | Controller | Reconciles LLMInferenceServiceConfig resources |\n92:| llmisvc | Go controller-runtime operator | cmd/llmisvc |\n125:| serving.kserve.io | v1alpha1, v1alpha2 | LLMInferenceService | Namespaced | Core API | Custom resource managed by kserve |\n126:| serving.kserve.io | v1alpha1, v1alpha2 | LLMInferenceServiceConfig | Namespaced | Core API | Custom resource managed by kserve |\n158:| /mutate-serving-kserve-io-v1alpha1-llminferenceservice | POST |  | HTTPS | Unknown | TLS | Kubernetes admission |  | Mutating admission webhook |\n159:| /mutate-serving-kserve-io-v1alpha2-llminferenceservice | POST |  | HTTPS | Unknown | TLS | Kubernetes admission |  | Mutating admission webhook |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f5be360b42a61fc","agent_id":"a074c867882eb1171","session_id":"207785e0-7a4d-4b13-b5f6-b50ef683c695","uuid":"ee995f95-b407-4b43-8365-774247a6355e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:02:02.907Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9324ac5bd5ef0eb7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8008 decomposition"}
